# Performance Optimization Rule

## AI Instructions

**This rule is designed for AI agents to follow. Always:**

- Focus on LOW-EFFORT, HIGH-IMPACT changes only
- Do NOT rewrite entire components
- Apply proven optimization patterns in 1-5 minutes max
- Only test the specific component being optimized
- Run `yarn validate` once at the very end
- **FOLLOW ALL CODE GUIDELINES** from @code-guidelines.mdc

## Code Guidelines Compliance

**All optimizations MUST follow these established patterns:**

- **TypeScript Strict Mode**: Always provide proper type annotations
- **Constants Usage**: Use `LAYOUT.SPACING`, `LAYOUT.ELEVATION`, `TYPOGRAPHY_HIERARCHY` from constants
- **Component Patterns**: Use `ThemedText`, `ThemedView`, `ThemedButton` for consistency
- **Import Patterns**: Use `import type` for type-only imports
- **Naming Conventions**: PascalCase for components, camelCase for functions
- **ESLint Compliance**: No unused variables, proper dependency arrays, no implicit any

## Performance Report Analysis

When you receive a performance report like:

```
LOG [PerfReport] App@(tabs) avg=48.0ms r=1 w=0 keys= | Screen:__root@(tabs) avg=48.0ms r=1 w=0 keys= | App@[id] avg=16.9ms r=207 w=0 keys= → Suggest: split heavy work/useMemo | Screen:/(tabs)/read/article/[id]@[id] avg=16.7ms r=207 w=0 keys= → Suggest: split heavy work/useMemo
```

**Key Metrics to Analyze:**

- `avg`: Average render time (target: <50ms for smooth 60fps)
- `r`: Re-render count (high counts indicate unnecessary re-renders)
- `w`: Write operations (should be minimal)
- `keys`: Cache keys (helps identify data dependencies)

## AI Investigation Process

### 1. Identify High Re-render Components

- Look for components with `r=207` (excessive re-renders)
- Check parent-child re-render relationships
- Identify components that re-render when parent re-renders

### 2. Root Cause Analysis

**Common Causes:**

- Props changing on every render (new object/function creation)
- Missing dependency arrays in useEffect/useCallback
- State updates triggering unnecessary re-renders
- Missing React.memo on expensive components
- Inline styles/objects being recreated

### 3. Check for Cascading Issues

**Before implementing fixes, verify:**

- No unintended side effects from previous optimizations
- State management isn't causing circular updates
- Redux selectors aren't creating new references
- Query cache invalidation isn't excessive

## AI Optimization Patterns (1-5 Minutes Each)

**IMPORTANT: These are the ONLY optimizations you should apply. Do NOT create new patterns.**

### 1. Quick React.memo Addition (5 seconds)

```tsx
// BEFORE: Component re-renders on every parent render
const ExpensiveComponent = ({ data }: { data: string[] }) => {
  return <ComplexChart data={data} />;
};

// AFTER: Simple memoization - just wrap in React.memo
const ExpensiveComponent = React.memo(({ data }: { data: string[] }) => {
  return <ComplexChart data={data} />;
});
```

### 2. Extract Static Constants (2-3 minutes)

```tsx
// BEFORE: Recreated on every render
const MyComponent = () => {
  const styles = StyleSheet.create({
    container: {
      padding: LAYOUT.SPACING.MEDIUM,
      margin: LAYOUT.SPACING.SMALL,
    },
  });

  return <View style={styles.container} />;
};

// AFTER: Move outside component - cut and paste
const STATIC_STYLES = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    padding: LAYOUT.SPACING.MEDIUM,
    margin: LAYOUT.SPACING.SMALL,
  },
});

const MyComponent = () => {
  return <View style={STATIC_STYLES.container} />;
};
```

### 3. Simple useMemo for Expensive Operations (1-2 minutes)

```tsx
// BEFORE: Calculation runs on every render
const MyComponent = ({ items }: { items: string[] }) => {
  const processedData = items.map(item => expensiveProcessing(item)).filter(Boolean);

  return <DataDisplay data={processedData} />;
};

// AFTER: Wrap existing calculation in useMemo
const MyComponent = ({ items }: { items: string[] }) => {
  const processedData = useMemo(
    () => items.map(item => expensiveProcessing(item)).filter(Boolean),
    [items]
  );

  return <DataDisplay data={processedData} />;
};
```

### 4. useCallback for Event Handlers (1 minute)

```tsx
// BEFORE: New function created on every render
const MyComponent = ({ onPress }: { onPress: () => void }) => {
  const handlePress = () => {
    onPress();
  };

  return <Button onPress={handlePress} />;
};

// AFTER: Wrap existing function in useCallback
const MyComponent = ({ onPress }: { onPress: () => void }) => {
  const handlePress = useCallback(() => {
    onPress();
  }, [onPress]);

  return <Button onPress={handlePress} />;
};
```

### 5. Style Memoization (1-2 minutes)

```tsx
// BEFORE: Styles recalculated on every render
const MyComponent = ({ isActive }: { isActive: boolean }) => {
  const styles = StyleSheet.create({
    container: {
      backgroundColor: isActive ? colors.tint : colors.background,
      padding: LAYOUT.SPACING.MEDIUM,
      elevation: LAYOUT.ELEVATION.SMALL,
    },
  });

  return <View style={styles.container} />;
};

// AFTER: Wrap StyleSheet.create in useMemo
const MyComponent = ({ isActive }: { isActive: boolean }) => {
  const styles = useMemo(
    () =>
      StyleSheet.create({
        container: {
          backgroundColor: isActive ? colors.tint : colors.background,
          padding: LAYOUT.SPACING.MEDIUM,
          elevation: LAYOUT.ELEVATION.SMALL,
        },
      }),
    [isActive]
  );

  return <View style={styles.container} />;
};
```

### 6. Memoize Expensive Calculations with Proper Types (1-2 minutes)

```tsx
// BEFORE: Expensive calculation without memoization
const MyComponent = ({
  items,
  filterValue,
}: {
  items: Array<{ id: string; value: number }>;
  filterValue: string;
}) => {
  const filteredItems = items
    .filter(item => item.value > 0)
    .sort((a, b) => b.value - a.value)
    .slice(0, 10);

  return <ItemList items={filteredItems} />;
};

// AFTER: Memoize with proper dependency array
const MyComponent = ({
  items,
  filterValue,
}: {
  items: Array<{ id: string; value: number }>;
  filterValue: string;
}) => {
  const filteredItems = useMemo(
    () =>
      items
        .filter(item => item.value > 0)
        .sort((a, b) => b.value - a.value)
        .slice(0, 10),
    [items, filterValue]
  );

  return <ItemList items={filteredItems} />;
};
```

### 7. Optimize List Rendering with FlashList (2-3 minutes)

```tsx
// BEFORE: ScrollView re-renders all items
const MyList = ({ items }: { items: Array<{ id: string; title: string }> }) => (
  <ScrollView>
    {items.map(item => (
      <ListItem key={item.id} item={item} />
    ))}
  </ScrollView>
);

// AFTER: FlashList with memoized items
const MyList = ({ items }: { items: Array<{ id: string; title: string }> }) => (
  <FlashList
    data={items}
    renderItem={({ item }) => <ListItem item={item} />}
    estimatedItemSize={100}
    keyExtractor={item => item.id}
  />
);

const ListItem = React.memo(({ item }: { item: { id: string; title: string } }) => (
  <View style={STATIC_STYLES.listItem}>
    <ThemedText style={TYPOGRAPHY_HIERARCHY.MEDIUM}>{item.title}</ThemedText>
  </View>
));
```

## AI Performance Thresholds

**Target Metrics:**

- **Render Time**: <50ms (16.67ms for 60fps)
- **Re-render Count**: <10 for stable components
- **Memory Usage**: Monitor for leaks during navigation

**Priority Levels:**

1. **Critical**: >100ms render time, >100 re-renders
2. **High**: 50-100ms render time, 50-100 re-renders
3. **Medium**: 30-50ms render time, 20-50 re-renders
4. **Low**: <30ms render time, <20 re-renders

## AI Validation Strategy

**During Development (NO TESTING):**

- [ ] **NEVER run individual component tests during optimization**
- [ ] **NEVER run yarn test or yarn test --testNamePattern during development**
- [ ] **NEVER run yarn test:coverage or any other test commands**
- [ ] Focus on functionality, not comprehensive coverage
- [ ] **ONLY run yarn validate at the very end**

**Final Validation (Only Once):**

- [ ] Run `yarn validate` at the very end
- [ ] This includes TypeScript, ESLint, and Knip checks
- [ ] **NO NEED to run individual validation commands during development**
- [ ] **NO NEED to test individual components during optimization**

